 Well, giraffes live in arid zones of Africa, very dry.

164
00:18:38,860 --> 00:18:43,440
 When grass becomes scarce, they eat leaves from treetops, which the other animals can't reach.

165
00:18:45,810 --> 00:18:51,570
 Many naturalists, like the Frenchman Lamarck, believe the giraffes acquire long necks because they stretch them,

166
00:18:51,650 --> 00:18:53,850
 and so their offspring are born with long necks.

167
00:18:54,030 --> 00:18:56,110
 But that's not how it happens. Not at all.

168
00:18:56,110 --> 00:19:01,420
 In every species of animal, and humans too, there are slight variations, hardly noticeable ones.

169
00:19:01,680 --> 00:19:05,720
 With a giraffe, when grass is scarce, the ones with longer necks are more fit to survive.

170
00:19:06,320 --> 00:19:07,800
